  "claimBoundary": [
    "success conformance is exact in straight-source and packed-premultiplied byte domains for static non-interlaced grayscale 1/2/4/8-bit, grayscale+alpha8, indexed 1/2/4/8-bit, RGB8 and RGBA8 sources with explicit sRGB authority, plus a separately bounded Adam7 RGBA8 slice; Adam7 cases cover full seven-pass geometry, empty-pass small images, every PNG filter, pass-local previous-row reset and split IDAT delivery; sub-byte grayscale/indexed rows are filtered in packed-byte form with bpp=1, PLTE is exercised from 2/3/11 entries through 256 entries, and out-of-range palette indices must fail closed",
    "truecolor PLTE is qualified only as a suggested palette and must not alter RGB/RGBA source samples or packed output; valid truecolor hIST is covered by package metamorphic/spec evidence, not this libpng pixel-success matrix, because libpng 1.6.58 reports it as out-of-place despite PNG Third Edition allowing it",
    "RGB8 and grayscale 1/2/4/8-bit tRNS are qualified as binary alpha with canonical unused high bits in the libpng success matrix; RGB8 composes with a suggested PLTE, while required grayscale unused-high-bit masking is locked separately by package/ImageIO differential tests because libpng 1.6.58 warns on non-zero unused high bits",
    "success cases carry explicit sRGB color authority; untagged and non-RGB ICC authority fail closed",
    "gAMA/cHRM and PNG Third Edition HDR metadata (mDCV/cLLI) remain outside the qualified domain even alongside sRGB; current-version reserved bits and color-authority ordering are enforced",
    "libpng is an independent pixel oracle and is not used as ImageCraft implementation code",
    "hostile cases must fail closed; error taxonomy is recorded but not widened to create support",
    "this profile does not publish PNGIndependentRGBA8Decoder as a production backend"
